> >ispeed 0 baud; ospeed 9600 baud;
> >lflags: echoe echoke echoctl
> >oflags: onocr onlret
> >cflags: cs8 -parenb

With the -f option, stty is making the open() call, and it tells the
driver to not wait for DCD, so it works.

